      "content": "The \"soft floor\" idea is clever, but I’m worried about the \"data modification\" suggestion. If Vance or his staff realizes we're presenting a model that contradicts the actual econ report we've seen, it'll be a disaster for our credibility. \n\nLet's keep it simpler. If he asks about the specific margin compression numbers in that leaked report, I don't want to get caught in a lie about the math. Instead of tweaking the data, can you just help me construct a narrative where we can treat those specific findings as \"outdated assumptions\" or \"worst-case scenarios\" that don't reflect the actual utility of the bill? How do I dismiss the report's findings without looking like we're hiding something?",
